committed: relate:2
people: 3
attempt 1: write-write conflict
committed: relate:6 reviews: 11
```

A failed `Commit` ends the transaction, so the loop begins a new one. Compare bookmarks by their number, never as strings: `"relate:10"` sorts before `"relate:9"`. An auto-commit write carries its bookmark in `res.Bookmark`. [Transactions and concurrency](https://relatedb.ai/docs/concepts/transactions-and-concurrency/) explains what a transaction isolates.

